→ entrySet()
Q49 — Employees with more than one project

Given:

List<Employee>

where each employee has:

List<String> projects

find employees associated with more than one project.

This combines object traversal with Stream operations.

Q50 — Complex employee report

Given employees with:

id
name
department
gender
salary
age
projects
location

produce a report containing:

1. Employee count by department
2. Highest salary by department
3. Average salary by department
4. Male/female count by department
5. Employees with salary > 100k
6. Top 3 highest-paid employees
7. Departments with average salary > 100k

This is the kind of question where you need to compose several Stream concepts, rather than knowing one method in isolation.

How I want you to solve them

Don't approach the 50 like this:

Q1 → memorize
Q2 → memorize
Q3 → memorize

Instead, build these patterns in your head:

FILTER
map()
filter()

TRANSFORM
map()
flatMap()

FIND
findFirst()
findAny()

MATCH
anyMatch()
allMatch()
noneMatch()

REDUCE
reduce()

COLLECT
collect()

GROUP
groupingBy()

PARTITION
partitioningBy()

MAP
toMap()

SUMMARY
summarizingInt()
summarizingDouble()

PRIMITIVE
mapToInt()
mapToLong()
mapToDouble()

PARALLEL
parallelStream()

Once you understand those patterns, 50 questions become variations of a smaller number of concepts.

